//// Decision 127 of 1.0.10-beta (front 24, § Cells "Migration"; guide.md § 9,
//// row `#[@context]` / `@Context<B, R>` as an effect) — an effect annotation that
//// had already left (decision 102 renamed it `#[@use]`, and 118 removed that)
//// stays gone. Measured at compiler `82e32e36`: `#[@context]` is accepted in
//// silence, as every unknown `#[@…]` annotation is. The cell asks for the
//// refusal of its family, `effect-annotation-removed` — the code the README's
//// table gives the six annotations; decision 127 says the older names "stay
//// gone" without naming a code, so this is the recommended reading, reported
//// as a choice. The new form is `run/component_hook_and_component.bp`.

pub type ElementBase()

#[@context]
fn state(initial: i32) -> @Component<ElementBase, i32> {
    return initial;
}

pub fn main() { state(1); }
